-- title:
--   Meromorphic Γ-invariant functions are quotients of modular forms
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a finite-index subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$ and let $F:\mathfrak H\to\mathbb C$ be a function on the upper half-plane subject to three hypotheses. First, meromorphy: for every $\tau\in\mathfrak H$ the function $z\mapsto F(\mathrm{ofComplex}\,z)$ on $\mathbb C$, where `ofComplex` is the retraction of $\mathbb C$ onto $\mathfrak H$, is meromorphic at the point $\tau$ regarded as a complex number. Second, invariance: $F(\gamma\cdot\tau)=F(\tau)$ for all $\gamma\in\Gamma$ and all $\tau\in\mathfrak H$. Third, exponential growth at every cusp: for each $\sigma\in\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$ there is a real constant $C$ with $\tau\mapsto F(\sigma\cdot\tau)$ of order $O\bigl(e^{C\,\operatorname{Im}\tau}\bigr)$ along the filter `atImInfty`. The conclusion provides an integer $k$ and two modular forms $g,h$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma$ (in Mathlib's sense, so holomorphic, weight-$k$ invariant under $\Gamma$ and of moderate growth at $\infty$ in all $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$-translates) with $h\neq 0$, such that for every $\tau\in\mathfrak H$ the functions $z\mapsto F(\mathrm{ofComplex}\,z)$ and $z\mapsto g(\mathrm{ofComplex}\,z)/h(\mathrm{ofComplex}\,z)$ agree on a punctured neighbourhood of $\tau$ in $\mathbb C$, i.e. eventually along the filter $\mathcal N[\neq]\,\tau$.
--
--   This is the classical statement that a meromorphic automorphic function of weight $0$ for a finite-index subgroup $\Gamma\le\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$, of at most exponential growth at the cusps, is locally the quotient of two holomorphic modular forms of a common weight for $\Gamma$; equivalently, the function field of the modular curve $X(\Gamma)$ is generated by such quotients. It is used in the formalisation to realise meromorphic invariant functions on modular curves of $\Gamma_H$-type as quotients of modular forms, via [`ModularCurve.exists_realizeOf_eventuallyEq_of_meromorphic_gammaH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_realizeOf_eventuallyEq_of_meromorphic_gammaH).
